<newsitem itemid="204641" id="root" date="1996-11-20" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Cable &amp; Wireless underlying H1 profits rise.</title>
<headline>Cable &amp; Wireless underlying H1 profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Sept 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		16.1		   vs 19.6</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.4		    vs 3.08</p>
<p> Pretax		     734		    vs 815</p>
<p> Turnover		   3,401		  vs 2,994</p>
<p>NOTE - Above results include exceptional profit of 61 million stg from AsiaSat flotation in current H1 and a 199 million stg profit in year-ago period. Pretax profit excluding exceptional items was 673 million stg in the current H1, up nine percent versus the year-ago.  </p>
<p>Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits excluding exceptionals were 650 to 668 million stg.</p>
<p> Operating profit	 746		    vs 636</p>
<p> Interest payable	 33		     vs 17</p>
<p> Tax			  153		    vs 190</p>
<p> Net taxed		  581		    vs 625</p>
<p> Attributable	     358		    vs 431</p>
<p> Pay date		   February 28, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  December 10</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
